      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "CHILLCUZ (4) hasn't won for a while but her recent form in better races has been commendable. Raced well in Victoria before returning to SA and catching the eye last start over this distance at Morphettville Parks. Has raced here once over 1400m and saluted - perfectly placed to double that tally. IMMORTAL SPIRIT (7) is the danger after a return to form at Gawler last Wednesday, beaten a whisker after attempting to lead all the way over 1500m. Draws a far better gate today and will be cherry ripe at the fourth run back. GRUELLING (3) missed the kick and failed to recover when resuming over 1200m at Murray Bridge recently. Races well here and the extra 200m is a tick. May still be one run short but should be competitive. MISS KASEI (6) has been poor in two runs this prep. Might be worth one more chance on a seven-day back-up with blinkers going on for the first time. UNPRAISED (5) can improve on a modest first-up effort in an unsuitable race.",
